course: dictionary
lesson: 2708
title: Dignity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dignity means that every person has worth, so they deserve respect. This is true even for someone you do not know, and even for someone who is struggling. «Kindness to people who are struggling, like buying a sandwich for a homeless man, treats people with dignity.»
explain: Dignity also means behaving in a calm, serious and proud way, even when times are hard. A character who keeps their head up after bad news is showing dignity. Ask yourself: is this person being treated with respect, or are they being used like a tool?
explain: The idea of human dignity is important in ethics, RE and citizenship lessons, and it is behind human rights. Look at the phrases «with dignity», «human dignity», «beneath my dignity» and «lose your dignity». The sentence around each one tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Dignity is the worth every person has, which means they should be treated with respect.
fact: «Immanuel Kant, a German philosopher of the 1700s, said everyone has dignity, so you must never just use a person like a ladder.»
fact: Kant taught that we should treat people as ends, never merely as means.
fact: Human dignity is the idea behind human rights.
fact: Dignity is uncountable, so we say «with dignity», not «a dignity».
exercise: Kant said everyone has dignity, so you must never just use a person like a ladder. What does dignity mean here? | Being the fastest runner | *The worth every person has, which means they should be respected | A loud, angry voice | The height of a building
exercise: «She walked into the hall with dignity, head high, even after losing the race.» What does dignity suggest? | Feeling sleepy | Running fast and shouting | Hiding from everyone | *Calm, serious pride even in hard times
exercise: Which phrase uses dignity to mean that something is below what you deserve? | Human dignity | *Beneath my dignity | With dignity | Gold dignity
test: Which sentence treats people with dignity? | *Buying a sandwich for a homeless man | Shouting at a stranger in the street | Ignoring someone who is struggling | Using a person like a ladder
test: What is the idea behind human rights? | Money in the bank | Being the tallest in the group | *Human dignity, the worth every person has | Strict borders and strong rules
exam: Kant said we should treat people as ends, never merely as means. What does this mean? | Use people whenever it helps you | Ends are finished, so forget people | Means are money, so pay people well | *Everyone has worth, so we must never just use them
